Input #0, mov,mp4,m4a,3gp,3g2,mj2, from '/Users/tydussimonini/Documents/Godot/PardonMe/Music/Ask for the Receipt.m4a':
  Metadata:
    major_brand     : isom
    minor_version   : 512
    compatible_brands: isomiso2mp41
    encoder         : Lavf60.16.100
    lyrics          : [Intro]
                    : Need the paperwork, please.
                    : No folklore without footnotes.
                    : [Hook]
                    : Ask for the receipt.
                    : Ask for the receipt.
                    : Who said it? When? Show me the sheet.
                    : Ask for the receipt.
                    : Ask for the receipt.
                    : Big talk gets small when the numbers meet.
                    : [Verse 1]
                    : He said he owned the corner, every brick had his name,
                    : But the landlord's got a ledger and it don't play the game.
                    : He said he bought the building, cash folded in a shoe,
                    : I asked for closing documents—he produced a menu.
                    : Claimed he ran the block since cassette tapes were new,
                    : But the barber's dated calendar says 'ninety-two.
                    : Said he never missed a rent, never borrowed a dime,
                    : Then a certified letter showed up right on time.
                    : He had a war story longer than a church basement pew,
                    : With twelve different witnesses and eleven points of view.
                    : I stayed polite, took notes, let the mythology speak,
                    : Then asked who signed the contract—he developed a leak.
                    : Not a drop on his jacket, not a stain on the floor,
                    : Just a sudden disappearance through a conveniently locked door.
                    : Your legend needs a witness, your victory needs a date,
                    : If the tale is truly heavy, it can carry its weight.
                    : [Hook]
                    : Ask for the receipt.
                    : Ask for the receipt.
                    : Who said it? When? Show me the sheet.
                    : Ask for the receipt.
                    : Ask for the receipt.
                    : Big talk gets small when the numbers meet.
                    : [Verse 2]
                    : He said he shipped a thousand units, platinum by noon,
                    : But the distributor's fax machine was still in the room.
                    : Said the label cut a check with a comma and a zero,
                    : I asked for the tax form—he pointed at a hero.
                    : Said he had a meeting with a suit from uptown,
                    : At a hotel with no lobby and a train station crown.
                    : He remembered every handshake, every cufflink shine,
                    : But couldn't name the Tuesday, couldn't locate the line.
                    : I brought timestamps, witness statements, ink that wouldn't fade,
                    : He brought a cousin's Polaroid of a lemonade.
                    : Serious as a judge, with a tie clipped to his shirt,
                    : Explaining how the money vanished due to international dirt.
                    : Yet his only foreign asset was a jar of imported tea,
                    : And the customs form described it as “two pounds, green.”
                    : I don't call him a liar; I audit what he said,
                    : Truth deserves a filing cabinet, not a rumor in your head.
                    : If the invoice says delivered, tell me who received,
                    : If the check was really cashed, show the bank that made you grieve.
                    : [Hook]
                    : Ask for the receipt.
                    : Ask for the receipt.
                    : Who said it? When? Show me the sheet.
                    : Ask for the receipt.
                    : Ask for the receipt.
                    : Big talk gets small when the numbers meet.
                    : [Verse 3]
                    : He said he won the battle with a verse that shook the floor,
                    : Had the whole room chanting before he touched the door.
                    : I asked for the promoter, asked the venue, asked the tape,
                    : He named a parking meter and a laundromat escape.
                    : Said the crowd was three hundred, maybe four if you count,
                    : But the fire-code report had a very different amount.
                    : Said the judge gave him the trophy, gold letters, heavyweight,
                    : The trophy shop remembered him ordering “participate.”
                    : He claimed the rival bowed, then retired on the spot,
                    : The rival's still performing with a freshly printed lot.
                    : I came with dates and witnesses, he came with confidence,
                    : Like a man who thinks a volume knob can substitute evidence.
                    : He cited one encyclopedia, page missing from the spine,
                    : Then blamed the public library for altering the line.
                    : Still, I never raised my voice; I sharpened every query,
                    : A clean record makes a tall tale unnecessary.
                    : Bring the contract, bring the docket, bring the person who was there,
                    : Bring the camera with the timestamp and the comb inside your hair.
                    : Because history isn't handed down by whoever talks the longest,
                    : The truth can wear a cheap suit and still be the strongest.
                    : [DJ Breakdown]
                    : Cut it up—
                    : Ask—ask—ask—
                    : For the re—re—receipt!
                    : Back to the facts.
                    : [Final Hook]
                    : Ask for the receipt.
                    : Ask for the receipt.
                    : Who said it? When? Show me the sheet.
                    : Ask for the receipt.
                    : Ask for the receipt.
                    : Big talk gets small when the numbers meet.
                    : Ask for the receipt.
                    : Ask for the receipt.
                    : Witness, timestamp, contract complete.
                    : Ask for the receipt.
                    : Ask for the receipt.
                    : Keep your legend honest when you step to the beat.
    comment         : made with suno; created=2026-09-04T08:26:59Z; id=7393854d-d374-4bbc-8f76-b3439a504a36
