Input #0, mov,mp4,m4a,3gp,3g2,mj2, from '/Users/tydussimonini/Documents/Godot/PardonMe/Music/The Devil Can't Drive My Truck.m4a':
  Metadata:
    major_brand     : isom
    minor_version   : 512
    compatible_brands: isomiso2mp41
    encoder         : Lavf60.16.100
    lyrics          : [Verse 1]
                    : I woke up with the sunrise
                    : And a receipt for what I’d done
                    : Dust on my old work boots
                    : And a prayer I hadn’t sung
                    : There was a map beneath the coffee
                    : With my bad years marked in red
                    : I turned the page toward mercy
                    : And let the past stay dead
                    : [Pre-Chorus]
                    : I heard a voice say, “Turn around”
                    : But I kept my hand on the door
                    : There’s a long road out of trouble
                    : And I’m not who I was before
                    : [Chorus]
                    : The Devil can’t drive my truck no more
                    : I threw his keys in the river by the county shore
                    : He left scorch marks on the passenger seat
                    : But grace came riding shotgun, keeping time with me
                    : I’ve got a new direction, a steadier heart
                    : A little less thunder when the engine starts
                    : I thank God for the road I’m headed toward
                    : The Devil can’t drive my truck no more
                    : [Verse 2]
                    : I found his old black hat there
                    : By the toolbox in the shed
                    : And a list of every midnight
                    : That I promised I’d forget
                    : I scrubbed the smoke from the window
                    : Till I could see the fields again
                    : Called my brother from the driveway
                    : And asked if we could start as friends
                    : [Pre-Chorus]
                    : He said, “You sound different, brother”
                    : I said, “I finally hear the truth”
                    : A man can spend a lifetime running
                    : Then turn around and choose
                    : [Chorus]
                    : The Devil can’t drive my truck no more
                    : I threw his keys in the river by the county shore
                    : He left scorch marks on the passenger seat
                    : But grace came riding shotgun, keeping time with me
                    : I’ve got a new direction, a steadier heart
                    : A little less thunder when the engine starts
                    : I thank God for the road I’m headed toward
                    : The Devil can’t drive my truck no more
                    : [Bridge]
                    : [Half-time, gospel-influenced]
                    : No more backseat bargains
                    : No more hands on the wheel
                    : No more calling wreckage
                    : Something I was born to feel
                    : If the water took those keys away
                    : Then let it carry off my name
                    : I’m not asking for an easy road
                    : Just strength to drive it straight
                    : [Final Chorus]
                    : The Devil can’t drive my truck no more
                    : I threw his keys in the river by the county shore
                    : He left scorch marks on the passenger seat
                    : But grace came riding shotgun, keeping time with me
                    : Now I’m taking the wheel, and I’m taking it slow
                    : With a choir in the cab and a place to go
                    : I thank God for the road I’m headed toward
                    : The Devil can’t drive my truck no more
                    : No, the Devil can’t drive my truck no more
                    : [Outro]
                    : The tires find the gravel
                    : The morning opens wide
                    : I’ve got both hands on the wheel now
                    : And peace beside me for the ride
    comment         : made with suno; created=2026-09-06T01:23:07Z; id=74a4d8ee-dc56-432f-814b-9aedd931913a
